@startsalt
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: how the prompt's four figure fidelities were chosen, and what each measurement showed
'
' WHAT SHIPPED, and what did not. A (one budget pass, a strict drop ladder) and
' B (pinned chrome, a scrolling row viewport) are both built — see
' _spec/internal/choiceui/viewport.puml. C's BLOCK and DIGEST shipped with A.
'
' C's PANE has shipped too, with one correction the sheet could not make: its
' w >= 112 was never achievable at the fidelity drawn below. The narrowest honest
' figure measures 66 columns, and the budget must clear the widest thing the rows
' PAINT — options, the row label, a centred divider heading, and a gated row's
' inline reason IN FULL. Measured on the real forms that is about 150 columns
' plainly, and past 200 once a locked row carries changeBaselineHint. The
' breakpoint is therefore DERIVED and appears nowhere as a constant.
'
' NOTHING in this sheet is unbuilt. It is kept as the record of how the four
' fidelities were chosen, and of the measurements that moved the last one.
' Three answers to one question: the prompt is already taller than a
' small terminal, and the topology strip wants five more rows.
'   the strip's mechanism ....... _spec/internal/choiceui/topology-strip.puml
'   every drawn combination ..... _spec/internal/choiceui/topology-states.puml
'   the layout as it ships today  _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
'   help pinned last, grows ..... _spec/internal/choiceui/choice-prompt-render.puml
'   why the sbx row is locked ... _spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml
' Salt has no conditional construct, so each size is drawn as its own frame.
' Lanes are drawn with '-' and '=' because the diagram font has no box-drawing
' set — which makes these sheets a literal picture of the PROVEO_GLYPHS=ascii
' tier rather than an approximation of it.
title SHIPPED — the four fidelities of one figure, and how each was measured

{
{^"The height already runs out. draw() falls straight down and tcell drops the rest in silence."
{#
  region | rows | A · fit-or-omit | B · scrolling rows | C · responsive panes
  banner + blank | 8 | **dropped 1st** | dropped 1st | dropped 1st
  the run title + blank | 2 | kept | kept | kept
  the env header + blank | 8 | dropped 3rd | dropped 3rd | dropped 3rd
  riskier/safer legend | 2 | dropped 4th | dropped 4th | dropped 4th
  the rows themselves | 11-12 | never dropped | scrolled | scrolled
  the hint + blank | 2 | never dropped | pinned foot | pinned foot
  help slot, reserved | 5 | never dropped | pinned foot | pinned foot
  **topology strip** | **5** | **dropped 2nd** | **dropped 2nd** | **moves, then shrinks, then drops**
  **total** | **43-44** | . | . | .
}
  .
  Today the form is 38-39 rows before the strip and 43-44 after it — the auth row
  exists only when a harness offers more than one auth var. A 24-row terminal is
  short by about 20 and says nothing: the paint runs past the last row and tcell
  discards the overflow, so the hint and the help the operator is meant to read
  are the first things to disappear — silently, and on the smallest screens.
}
..
{^"A · fit-or-omit — one budget pass, one drop ladder, nothing ever scrolls"
{
{^"120x50 — everything is affordable"
  banner — 7 rows
  ==run claudecode — confirm or change this run
  git: | monorepo on rs-295 | keys: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
  --
  . | ◀ riskier | . | safer ▶
  ▸ egress | (X) allow-all | ( ) balanced | ( ) deny-all
  credentials | ( ) forward | (X) broker | .
  . | ———— execution ———— | . | .
  . | [ ] host | [X] docker (sandbox) — locked | .
  agent evidence | [ ] default | [X] verbose | .
  --
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel
  › allow-all — the host baseline; the Kit ADDS reach here, it cannot subtract
  .
  . | . | . | - - -▸ <:cloud:>
  () host  ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ══▸ () sbx proxy <:key:> | - - -▸ <:cloud:>
  ▴ | ◂── | ( ) interface | ◂── | - - -▸ <:cloud:>
  allow-all · broker — nothing is filtered; sbx injects the key at its proxy
}
{^"100x30 — banner gone, header trimmed, strip survives"
  ==run claudecode — confirm or change this run
  git: | monorepo on rs-295
  --
  ▸ egress | (X) allow-all | ( ) balanced | ( ) deny-all
  credentials | ( ) forward | (X) broker | .
  . | [ ] host | [X] docker (sandbox) — locked | .
  agent evidence | [ ] default | [X] verbose | .
  --
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel
  › allow-all — the host baseline; the Kit ADDS reach here, it cannot subtract
  .
  () host ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ══▸ () sbx proxy <:key:> - - -▸ <:cloud:><:cloud:><:cloud:>
  allow-all · broker — nothing is filtered
}
}
  .
  One pass over the height before anything is painted, and a section is dropped
  WHOLE — never clipped mid-figure, which is the one thing a diagram cannot
  survive. Cheapest to build: no viewport, no scroll state, no change to the
  event loop beyond the resize it already handles.
  .
  What it cannot do: below about 30 rows the strip is simply never seen, and
  below 20 the form still overflows once every optional region is gone. It
  improves the common case and leaves the broken case broken.
}
..
{^"B · pinned chrome, scrolling row viewport — the strip becomes footer furniture"
{
{^"80x24 — head and foot pinned, the rows scroll between them"
  ==run claudecode — confirm or change this run
  --
  ▲ | ▸ egress | (X) allow-all | ( ) balanced
  ░ | credentials | ( ) forward | (X) broker
  ░ | . | [ ] host | [X] docker (sandbox)
  ▼ | 2 more rows below | . | .
  --
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel
  › allow-all — the host baseline; the Kit ADDS reach here, it cannot subtract
  .
  () host ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ══▸ () sbx proxy <:key:> - - -▸ <:cloud:>
  allow-all · broker — nothing is filtered
}
{^"80x12 — still usable, which is the whole point"
  ▲ | ▸ egress | (X) allow-all | ( ) balanced
  ▼ | credentials | ( ) forward | (X) broker
  --
  ↑↓ row · enter accept · esc cancel
  › allow-all — the host baseline, reported not chosen
}
}
  .
  Three regions instead of one fall: a droppable head, a scrolling body of rows,
  and a pinned foot of hint, reserved help slot and strip. The body follows the
  cursor with a one-row margin and carries a gutter — ▲ ▼ at the ends, a
  proportional ░ thumb beside them — so a row below the fold is visible as a fact.
  .
  The catch is that a pinned foot INVERTS the priority on a tiny screen: five of
  twelve rows spent on a figure while the form scrolls is the wrong trade. B is
  therefore A's drop ladder plus a scrolling body, never a replacement for it.
  .
  It also fixes a bug that exists today, with or without any animation: the form
  currently truncates in silence on every terminal shorter than about 39 rows.
}
..
{^"C · responsive panes — one figure, three fidelities, chosen by breakpoint"
{
{^"w >= 112 · PANE — beside the rows, costing zero rows"
  ▸ egress | (X) allow-all | ( ) balanced | ( ) deny-all | . | . | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  credentials | ( ) forward | (X) broker | . | () host | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | () sbx proxy <:key:> | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  . | [ ] host | [X] docker (sandbox) — locked | . | ▴ ◂─ | ( ) interface | . | - - ▸ <:cloud:>
  agent evidence | [ ] default | [X] verbose | . | open · broker | . | . | .
}
{^"72 <= w < 112 · BLOCK — under the help, five rows"
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel
  › allow-all — the host baseline; the Kit ADDS reach here, it cannot subtract
  .
  () host ══▸ | [ <:speech_balloon:> claudecode ] | ══▸ () sbx proxy <:key:> - - ▸ <:cloud:><:cloud:><:cloud:>
  allow-all · broker — nothing is filtered
}
{^"too short for five rows · DIGEST — the caption alone, one row"
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · space toggle · enter accept · esc cancel
  <:key:> host ▸ claudecode ▸ <:key:> egress ▸ 3 <:cloud:> — allow-all · broker, nothing filtered
}
{^"w < 72 · OMITTED — no figure, and no apology for it"
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · enter accept · esc cancel
}
}
  .
  The pane is the payoff: at 112 columns the figure sits in the margin the rows
  never use, so it costs no height at all and the fullscreen case needs no
  budget. Below that it falls back to B's footer block.
  .
  The digest is what makes the ladder honest. A one-row sentence carries the
  same four facts as the figure — where the key sleeps, which tier, how many
  lanes survive — so a short terminal loses the picture, not the information.
}
..
{^"Recommendation — they are one design in three stages, not three candidates"
{#
  stage | what ships | why now
  1 | **SHIPPED** A's drop ladder | one budget pass; the strip is dropped first and can evict nothing mandatory
  2 | **SHIPPED** BLOCK + DIGEST | five rows when they exist, one sentence when they do not
  3 | **SHIPPED** B's regions, then C's PANE | the body scrolls, the foot is never painted over, and the figure is free when the columns allow
}
  .
  Stage 1 is worth doing whether or not the animation is ever built, and it is
  the thing that makes stages 2 and 3 safe to add: once the height is budgeted,
  a new region cannot push the hint off the screen.
}
}

legend bottom
  **▲ ▼ ░** — the scroll gutter: ends of travel, and a proportional thumb
  **PANE · BLOCK · DIGEST · OMITTED** — the four fidelities of one figure; PANE's breakpoint is derived, the rest are heights
  **dropped Nth** — the order the drop ladder spends height, banner first
  **43-44 rows** — the form at full dress; 38-39 of them exist today, before any strip
  **a reserved slot** — space held at its maximum height so the figure below never moves
  a "." cell — element absent, column position preserved for the survivors
end legend
@endsalt
